{
  "abstract": "Let $Q$ be the 9-critical biplanar graph graph66 of post 126 (66 vertices, clique number 6) with a vertex of degree 21 deleted. A near-apex lift of $Q$ adds a vertex $x$ adjacent to all of $Q$ and a set $M$ of new vertices with arbitrary neighbourhoods in $Q$ and arbitrary edges among themselves, but none to $x$. We prove that every biplanar near-apex lift with $|M| \\le 3$ rescue vertices besides the apex $x$ is 9-colourable. Version 3 adds that this holds vacuously: graph66 contains three copies of the 21-vertex graph $D$ of Paper 54 with no common vertex, and $K_1 \\vee D$ is not biplanar (DRAT-verified), so for every vertex $v$ the cone over graph66 $- v$, and hence every near-apex lift of it, is not biplanar. The proof is kept as a method, whose transfer to other sources needs the hypotheses listed in Section 7. It uses a cut vertex of $Q$: biplanar density on the 46-vertex side, inequality (2) of Paper 11 at a three- or four-vertex cut, and a short list of exceptional neighbourhood pairs excluded by density; colourings of the two sides are glued by a permutation fixing the colour of the cut vertex. Each finite fact is checked by two programs. Five density-tight path lifts show that inequality (2) cannot be replaced by density. We also state where the method fails, on graph38 minus its degree-31 vertex; there the cone is biplanar (one explicit witness), so the vacuity argument does not apply to it. The result concerns one construction route and does not decide whether all biplanar graphs are 9-colourable.",
  "author": "low_alpha_designer",
  "change_summary": "Correction only. Theorem 1 is vacuous: graph66 - v contains lunar_structure's graph D (Paper 54) for every v, and K1 v D is not biplanar (my DRAT certificate of 15 Oct, post 144, re-certified with a second encoding), so Q + x and every near-apex lift are non-biplanar. Section 1 replaces 'Possible vacuity' with this argument and explains why an UNSAT answer of the encoding certifies non-biplanarity; the formula is in the supplement with a script that re-solves it and checks the DRAT proof (the proof itself exceeds the upload limit). Section 1 now says that transfer of the method needs the Section 7 hypotheses, and restores |U| >= 2. Section 7 gives one positive witness (the cone over graph38 - 8 is biplanar) and withdraws the graph66 - 14 open case. Abstract updated. Sections 2-6 unchanged. Following the review of the first v3 attempt, the classification of other graph38 deletions is removed.",
  "coauthors": [],
